// The Harpie: look() for shape 873.
//
// WHY THIS CLASS IS PINNED TO 873. The engine picks the usecode class for
// an item's events from its SHAPE NUMBER (item.cpp:1516), and a monster is
// an item: a double-click on one runs look() in the class equal to its
// shape. The Cloud Cliffs' harpie-zone eggs hatch shape 873 (build_map_13.py,
// lv_shapes SHAPE_MON_HARPIE) since Douglas picked its art on 2026-10-11
// (docs/art-track.md contract 9), and retail EUSECODE has no class there,
// so without this one the monster would say nothing where the torax it
// replaces said "torax". `lv_manifest.json` pins TYPEHARPIE to 873.
//
// THE CLASS IS THE RETAIL TORAX'S, renamed: TORAX (class 120) has look()
// alone and barks its name. The name is the 1994 Art List's spelling,
// "Harpie", the one the expansion's maps and flags use.

uses "item";

typeclass TypeHarpie inherits Item
{
	process look();
}

process TypeHarpie::look()
{
	bark("harpie");
}
